      "writtenOn": "2022-09-30T17:42:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I worry that this makes this sound like a hack, where we want to assert \"actually, this is correct still, and here\u0027s why.\" I think that the comment here should focus more on describing the other mechanisms that make this unnecessary, perhaps with an example.\n\nThe way I\u0027d describe it is that PlantSymlinkForest will have the same effect regardless of contents of the directories, **except** for BUILD.bazel files contained in the directory. Thus only BUILD.bazel files belong in ninjaDeps.\n\nYou can also mention that BUILD.bazel file dependencies are captured by finder.\n\nFWIW, I do like the description for why adding each child directory would cause superfluous rebuilds (and the IDE example).",
      "revId": "2b295d5a44711bc3f22632ab7c9ca434f01360ee",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7e6501ec_d16b66ed",
        "filename": "cmd/soong_build/main.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 554,
      "author": {
        "id": 1535516
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-30T17:52:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I mean, it is a hack. This will reduce the correctness of bp2build, and cause incremental bp2build\u0027s to sometimes fail. (In the case of adding/removing an implicitly referenced file like AndroidManifest.xml) We don\u0027t have other mechanisms that replace this.\n\nI would argue we shouldn\u0027t make this change because of that.\n\nHowever, I too have noticed how frequently bp2build reruns for apparently no reason. If those \"random\" reruns are caused by this dependency, maybe we could figure out which folders are changing, and why, and just ignore those folder if they\u0027re special in some way?",
      "parentUuid": "d9e806a6_207697f5",
      "revId": "2b295d5a44711bc3f22632ab7c9ca434f01360ee",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "09038687_1b7c7d08",
        "filename": "cmd/soong_build/main.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 554,
      "author": {
        "id": 1605027
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-30T18:07:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\"This is a hack because it may reduce the correctness of bp2build\" is a false equivalence. This may be closer to \"doing the right thing\" here, but unearth some larger correctness issues of the build system.\n\nIf there are several places you anticipate this will disturb correctness, lets talk about them. In the case of implicit AndroidManifest.xml dependencies: this is a correctness issue already present in Soong, IIUC. If it\u0027s going to be fixed anywhere, it should be fixed there (in finder.go, presumably). This correctness issue barely even gets noticed by our users, AFAIK.\n\n`b` correctness will be no worse than legacy correctness as a result of this CL, and incremental performance should drastically improve. If we want to improve correctness of both build systems, we should do that in a followup.\n\n\u003e maybe we could figure out which folders are changing, and why, and just ignore those folder if they\u0027re special in some way?\n\nThis would be a hackier solution, if I understand you correctly: denylisting certain directories from ninjaDeps because we anticipate they\u0027re volatile. Instead, we should be depending on the exact set of things that would change the outputs of bp2build; bp2build should only retrigger on elements which affect the output of the generated symlink forest or the BUILD files generated.",
      "parentUuid": "7e6501ec_d16b66ed",
      "revId": "2b295d5a44711bc3f22632ab7c9ca434f01360ee",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f5afc4e1_ceafcfdc",
        "filename": "cmd/soong_build/main.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
